    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-koto-wa-ga",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "The pattern repeats the SAME predicate on both sides of ことは (casual verb + ことは + the same verb + が; i-adjective + ことは + the same i-adjective + が; na-adjective + na + ことは + the same na-adjective + だが; noun + ことは + the same noun + だが). The op enum transforms one base and appends fixed literal tokens; it has no operation that re-emits the base, and an append token cannot vary with the input, so no ordered sequence can produce the second copy. A single-copy sequence would emit 高いことは / 書くことは, which is not this point. Note also that this record's structure_pattern and forms[0].form are themselves corrupted with an editing instruction in place of the pattern (failure mode F6), so only the formation prose was usable here.",
      "nuance_tags": [
        "concession",
        "softening"
      ],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "spoken",
        "written"
      ]
    },
