    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-kurai-wa-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Two-slot frame whose closing half is an open clause, not a fixed token. The record specifies the opening half exactly (noun / number / plain verb + くらい + は) but then says the frame closes with a negative clause OR with 〜ないと, i.e. free material no append token can stand for. A sequence ending at くらいは would emit 週に一度くらいは and silently drop the obligatory negative that carries this point's whole meaning, teaching plain くらい + は instead. Note also that this record's structure_pattern and forms[0].form are corrupted with an editing instruction in place of the pattern (failure mode F6); only the formation prose was usable.",
      "nuance_tags": [
        "emphasis",
        "obligation"
