    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-mattaku-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix around a fixed pre-predicate adverb: the record's own formation is 'place まったく before the predicate, which must be negative' (まったく覚えていない, まったく暖かくない, まったく静かではない). The closed op set has append and no prepend, so a sequence from one base could only emit the negative half — 書かない, 高くない, 静かではない — which is the plain negative, dropping the まったく slot that is this point's entire content.",
      "nuance_tags": [
        "emphasis"
      ],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "spoken",
        "written"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-metta-ni-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix around a fixed pre-predicate adverb: めったに opens and the predicate must go negative (めったに外食しない, めったに高くない, めったに静かではない); the record states that めったに with an affirmative verb is incorrect. With append and no prepend in the op enum, any sequence would emit only the negative half (外食しない), which is the plain negative and carries none of the 'rarely' meaning that めったに supplies.",
      "nuance_tags": [
        "emphasis"
